  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed two‑storey side extension would erode the openness of this prominent corner plot, appear disproportionate and overly dominant in relation to the host dwelling and the wider semi‑detached pair, and create an unbalanced appearance through the loss of symmetry and uniformity. In addition, the fenestration is poorly considered and fails to reflect the established character of the dwelling, the semi‑detached pair, and the wider Becontree Estate.&nbsp;&nbsp;The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character and historic distinctiveness:National Planning Policy Framework (MHCLG) (December, 2024)Policies D4 and&nbsp;HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1, DMD4&nbsp;and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)&nbsp;"
